       --ss, ----ssiinnccee _t_i_m_e
           Display the state of logins since the specified _t_i_m_e. This is
           useful, e.g., to easily determine who was logged in at a particular
           time. The option is often combined with ----uunnttiill.

       --tt, ----uunnttiill _t_i_m_e
           Display the state of logins until the specified _t_i_m_e.

       ----ttiimmee--ffoorrmmaatt _f_o_r_m_a_t
           Define the output timestamp _f_o_r_m_a_t to be one of _n_o_t_i_m_e, _s_h_o_r_t,
           _f_u_l_l, or _i_s_o. The _n_o_t_i_m_e variant will not print any timestamps at
           all, _s_h_o_r_t is the default, and _f_u_l_l is the same as the ----ffuullllttiimmeess
           option. The _i_s_o variant will display the timestamp in ISO-8601
